  "claim_boundary": "Structural storage-accounting evidence on declared banks in one interpreter. Byte counts depend on the CPython build and use the declared interpreter tolerance; counts and packed bytes remain exact. The measured ladder locates observed 3x crossings but does not establish a universal reuse threshold. Historical molecular records preserve T_coeff/W_selected, an upper bound on resident reuse, and cannot establish savings on those banks. This record does not grade streaming or process feasibility, or establish that Phase 2M passes.",
  "committed_bank_reuse": {
    "caveat": "These are resident coefficients per *selected-subspace* word, not true coefficient reuse: the committed records preserved the selected subspace's W and not the word union of the rejected rows still in their caches, as Phase 2M-A's own reuse_recovery_boundary records. The resident universe is the larger of the two, so true reuse is no greater than the ratio quoted here. That direction matters: it means these numbers may overstate where those banks sit on the ladder. They cannot establish that any historical bank clears 3x.",
    "ratio_range": [
      35.112119493287956,
      154.86022576361222
    ],
