    "statement": "Interleaved keeps one complex128 array and structure-of-arrays keeps separate float64 real and imaginary arrays; both are sixteen bytes per coefficient, so the choice between them is one of access cost and not of size. The byte equality is checked here rather than assumed, because a layout that silently changed the footprint would make every reduction below ambiguous about which representation produced it."
